      <b>ECON 5613</b> - Econometrics I [<A id="title_ca"  HREF="courses/econ5613/econ5613_syl.pdf" onClick="javascript: _gaq.push(['_trackPageview', '/downloads/papers/relcoop']);">Syllabus</A>]</p>
      <div class="abstract" style="display:block" id="brief_ca">
        This course offers a rigorous, but intuitive, graduate-level introduction to econometrics that provides a foundation for users of econometrics to begin engaging in applied research and to take more advanced coursework.
        <br>
        <br><b>Textbooks:</b>
        <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="http://people.stern.nyu.edu/wgreene/Text/econometricanalysis.htm" target="new window">Greene (2012). <i>Econometric Analysis, 7E</i></a> (main)
        <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="http://mitpress.mit.edu/books/econometric-analysis-cross-section-and-panel-data" target="new window">Wooldridge (2010). <i>Econometric Analysis of Cross Section and Panel Data, 2E</i></a> (supplementary)
      </div>
